{"v":15,"id":"e10","kid":"emma","title":"Helen Keller","zh":"海伦·凯勒","level":"B1","genre":"人物传记","src":"facts","sum":"海伦·凯勒幼年因病失明失聪。老师安妮·沙利文在她手心拼写单词，她在水泵旁明白了\"water\"。后来她大学毕业，一生为残障人士争取权利。","words":297,"paras":[{"t":"When Helen Keller was born in Alabama, USA, in 1880, she was a healthy baby. But when she was about nineteen months old, a serious illness left her unable to see or hear. Because she could not hear words, she could not learn to speak. As she grew older, she became angry and wild. She often kicked, screamed and broke things. Her family did not know how to help her.","w":[[0,4,"when",-1],[5,10,"Helen",-1],[11,17,"Keller",-1],[18,21,"was",-1],[22,26,"born",-1],[27,29,"in",-1],[30,37,"Alabama",-1],[39,42,"USA",-1],[44,46,"in",-1],[53,56,"she",-1],[57,60,"was",-1],[61,62,"a",-1],[63,70,"healthy",-1],[71,75,"baby",-1],[77,80,"but",-1],[81,85,"when",-1],[86,89,"she",-1],[90,93,"was",-1],[94,99,"about",-1],[100,108,"nineteen",-1],[109,115,"months",-1],[116,119,"old",-1],[121,122,"a",-1],[123,130,"serious",-1],[131,138,"illness",-1],[139,143,"left",-1],[144,147,"her",-1],[148,154,"unable",-1],[155,157,"to",-1],[158,161,"see",-1],[162,164,"or",-1],[165,169,"hear",-1],[171,178,"because",-1],[179,182,"she",-1],[183,188,"could",-1],[189,192,"not",-1],[193,197,"hear",-1],[198,203,"words",-1],[205,208,"she",-1],[209,214,"could",-1],[215,218,"not",-1],[219,224,"learn",-1],[225,227,"to",-1],[228,233,"speak",-1],[235,237,"as",-1],[238,241,"she",-1],[242,246,"grew",-1],[247,252,"older",-1],[254,257,"she",-1],[258,264,"became",-1],[265,270,"angry",-1],[271,274,"and",-1],[275,279,"wild",-1],[281,284,"she",-1],[285,290,"often",-1],[291,297,"kicked",-1],[299,307,"screamed",-1],[308,311,"and",-1],[312,317,"broke",-1],[318,324,"things",-1],[326,329,"her",-1],[330,336,"family",-1],[337,340,"did",-1],[341,344,"not",-1],[345,349,"know",-1],[350,353,"how",-1],[354,356,"to",-1],[357,361,"help",-1],[362,365,"her",-1]]},{"t":"In 1887, when Helen was six, a young teacher named Anne Sullivan came to live with the family. Anne had poor eyesight herself, so she understood some of Helen's difficulties. She began to spell words into Helen's hand with her fingers. She spelled \"d-o-l-l\" while Helen held a doll, but Helen did not understand that the movements were words.","w":[[0,2,"in",-1],[9,13,"when",-1],[14,19,"Helen",-1],[20,23,"was",-1],[24,27,"six",-1],[29,30,"a",-1],[31,36,"young",-1],[37,44,"teacher",-1],[45,50,"named",-1],[51,55,"Anne",-1],[56,64,"Sullivan",-1],[65,69,"came",-1],[70,72,"to",-1],[73,77,"live",-1],[78,82,"with",-1],[83,86,"the",-1],[87,93,"family",-1],[95,99,"Anne",-1],[100,103,"had",-1],[104,108,"poor",1],[109,117,"eyesight",1],[118,125,"herself",-1],[127,129,"so",-1],[130,133,"she",-1],[134,144,"understood",-1],[145,149,"some",-1],[150,152,"of",-1],[153,160,"helen's",-1],[161,173,"difficulties",-1],[175,178,"she",-1],[179,184,"began",-1],[185,187,"to",-1],[188,193,"spell",-1],[194,199,"words",-1],[200,204,"into",-1],[205,212,"helen's",-1],[213,217,"hand",-1],[218,222,"with",-1],[223,226,"her",-1],[227,234,"fingers",-1],[236,239,"she",-1],[240,247,"spelled",-1],[249,256,"d-o-l-l",-1],[258,263,"while",-1],[264,269,"Helen",-1],[270,274,"held",-1],[275,276,"a",-1],[277,281,"doll",-1],[283,286,"but",-1],[287,292,"Helen",-1],[293,296,"did",-1],[297,300,"not",-1],[301,311,"understand",-1],[312,316,"that",-1],[317,320,"the",-1],[321,330,"movements",-1],[331,335,"were",-1],[336,341,"words",-1]]},{"t":"The big moment came one day at the water pump. Anne held one of Helen's hands under the cool, running water and spelled \"w-a-t-e-r\" into the other. Suddenly Helen understood: the shapes in her hand were the name of the wonderful cool thing flowing over her skin. Everything had a name! By that evening, she had learned thirty words.","w":[[0,3,"the",-1],[4,7,"big",2],[8,14,"moment",2],[15,19,"came",-1],[20,23,"one",-1],[24,27,"day",-1],[28,30,"at",-1],[31,34,"the",-1],[35,40,"water",0],[41,45,"pump",0],[47,51,"Anne",-1],[52,56,"held",-1],[57,60,"one",-1],[61,63,"of",-1],[64,71,"helen's",-1],[72,77,"hands",-1],[78,83,"under",-1],[84,87,"the",-1],[88,92,"cool",-1],[94,101,"running",-1],[102,107,"water",-1],[108,111,"and",-1],[112,119,"spelled",-1],[121,130,"w-a-t-e-r",-1],[132,136,"into",-1],[137,140,"the",-1],[141,146,"other",-1],[148,156,"suddenly",-1],[157,162,"Helen",-1],[163,173,"understood",-1],[175,178,"the",-1],[179,185,"shapes",-1],[186,188,"in",-1],[189,192,"her",-1],[193,197,"hand",-1],[198,202,"were",-1],[203,206,"the",-1],[207,211,"name",-1],[212,214,"of",-1],[215,218,"the",-1],[219,228,"wonderful",-1],[229,233,"cool",-1],[234,239,"thing",-1],[240,247,"flowing",-1],[248,252,"over",-1],[253,256,"her",-1],[257,261,"skin",-1],[263,273,"everything",-1],[274,277,"had",-1],[278,279,"a",-1],[280,284,"name",-1],[286,288,"by",-1],[289,293,"that",-1],[294,301,"evening",-1],[303,306,"she",-1],[307,310,"had",-1],[311,318,"learned",-1],[319,325,"thirty",-1],[326,331,"words",-1]]},{"t":"After that, Helen learned quickly. She learned to read Braille, a system of raised dots that blind people read with their fingers. She also learned to write and, later, to speak. In 1904, she graduated from Radcliffe College. She was the first deaf and blind person in the United States to earn a university degree.","w":[[0,5,"after",-1],[6,10,"that",-1],[12,17,"Helen",-1],[18,25,"learned",-1],[26,33,"quickly",-1],[35,38,"she",-1],[39,46,"learned",-1],[47,49,"to",-1],[50,54,"read",-1],[55,62,"Braille",-1],[64,65,"a",-1],[66,72,"system",-1],[73,75,"of",-1],[76,82,"raised",-1],[83,87,"dots",-1],[88,92,"that",-1],[93,98,"blind",-1],[99,105,"people",-1],[106,110,"read",-1],[111,115,"with",-1],[116,121,"their",-1],[122,129,"fingers",-1],[131,134,"she",-1],[135,139,"also",-1],[140,147,"learned",-1],[148,150,"to",-1],[151,156,"write",-1],[157,160,"and",-1],[162,167,"later",-1],[169,171,"to",-1],[172,177,"speak",-1],[179,181,"in",-1],[188,191,"she",-1],[192,201,"graduated",3],[202,206,"from",3],[207,216,"Radcliffe",5],[217,224,"c